1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,089
Every coach talks about pressing. But ask which parts of your press actually create

2
00:00:05,089 --> 00:00:10,179
chances, and most staff can't really tell you. That's the question Turnover Map answers.

3
00:00:10,629 --> 00:00:15,853
Pick a team. This is Leicester, in their title-winning season. About thirty-five open-play regains

4
00:00:15,853 --> 00:00:21,449
a match, and more expected goals from those regains than anyone else in the league.

5
00:00:21,899 --> 00:00:29,150
First, the coach's notes, in plain English. Where winning the ball pays off, where it tends to go nowhere, and where losing

6
00:00:29,150 --> 00:00:36,729
it hurts the most. And every note only uses zones with at least thirty turnovers, so nothing's built on a handful of moments.

7
00:00:37,179 --> 00:00:42,782
Here's the heart of it. Each zone is coloured by what a regain there was actually worth, not by

8
00:00:42,782 --> 00:00:48,679
how many there were. The hatched zones just don't have enough data yet, and we'd rather say that than guess.

9
00:00:49,129 --> 00:00:53,394
Tap any zone for the detail. Right-centre, just past halfway: fifty

10
00:00:53,394 --> 00:00:57,659
regains, and one in five became a shot inside ten seconds.

11
00:00:58,109 --> 00:01:01,929
Switch to the league comparison, and you can see where this team gets

12
00:01:01,929 --> 00:01:05,749
more than an average side would, from the very same patch of grass.

13
00:01:06,199 --> 00:01:09,604
Turn on the chains, and every regain that led to a shot

14
00:01:09,604 --> 00:01:13,009
is drawn on the pitch. The orange ones ended in a goal.

15
00:01:13,459 --> 00:01:21,392
Now, an honest check. Leicester's regains were worth far more when they were already winning, because teams chasing the game leave space behind

16
00:01:21,392 --> 00:01:29,669
them. So part of this pattern is the scoreline, not only the press. We treat it as a correlation, never as cause and effect.

17
00:01:30,119 --> 00:01:35,209
Kanté wins the ball more than anyone in the squad. And across the league, Leicester sit well

18
00:01:35,209 --> 00:01:40,299
above the pack on value per regain. You can tap any dot to jump to that team.

19
00:01:40,749 --> 00:01:44,712
For the video analyst, every one of those chains is listed with the

20
00:01:44,712 --> 00:01:48,979
match and the minute, best chances first, and it exports straight to a spreadsheet.

21
00:01:49,429 --> 00:01:54,860
It's all precomputed from StatsBomb open data, so it loads instantly, works on a phone, and

22
00:01:54,860 --> 00:02:00,629
the full table is right there for anyone who wants to check the work. That's Turnover Map.
